<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudd Concession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1888</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rudd Concession was a document signed in October 1888 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobengula">Lobengula</a>, granting exclusive mining rights in his lands to agents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a> led by Charles Rudd. Lobengula later said he had been deceived about its terms. It was the basis for the royal charter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> in 1889 and its occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mashonaland">Mashonaland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudd-concession.jpg" alt="Rudd Concession" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Rudd (died 1916) and Lobengula Kumalo (died 1894) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rudd_Concession.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
